## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the TMPlayer static website.

### What was implemented:

1. **Fetched latest documentation**: Retrieved the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart to ensure we used the most up-to-date installation method.

2. **Identified project structure**: Determined that this is a vanilla HTML/JavaScript static website without a build system, located in the `site/` directory with 8 HTML pages.

3. **Implemented CDN-based analytics**: Added the Vercel Web Analytics script tag to all HTML pages using the recommended CDN approach for static sites:
   ```html
   <!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
   <script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
   ```

### Files modified:

- `site/index.html` - Home page
- `site/download/index.html` - Download page
- `site/features/index.html` - Features page
- `site/faq/index.html` - FAQ page
- `site/android-tv/index.html` - Android TV page
- `site/install/index.html` - Installation guide page
- `site/legal/index.html` - Legal information page
- `site/privacy/index.html` - Privacy policy page

### Implementation details:

- The analytics script was added in the `<head>` section of each page, right after the stylesheet link and before other inline scripts
- Used the `defer` attribute to ensure non-blocking page load performance
- The script uses the official Vercel CDN (cdn.vercel-insights.com)
- All existing code structure and formatting was preserved

### Why this approach:

For static HTML sites without a build system, Vercel recommends using the CDN script tag approach rather than the npm package. This method:
- Works seamlessly with Vercel deployments
- Requires no build step or dependencies
- Automatically tracks page views across all pages
- Maintains excellent performance with the deferred loading

### Next steps for the user:

1. Deploy the site to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Once deployed, verify analytics are working by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/`
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation and is production-ready.
